## Dead Ends
Calling dist.all_reduce directly on the replicated DTensor was rejected by PyTorch 2.11. Converting optimizer parameters or found_inf permanently to local tensors was rejected because fused AdamW expects the existing DTensor optimizer state and placement contract.

## Hints for Future Agents
The local tensor returned by DTensor.to_local shares the outer scalar's storage for this replicated found_inf value. Reduce that local view across the already initialized training process group, then pass the original DTensor to fused AdamW. The exact FULL_SHARD run must still prove the optimizer update and checkpoint save.

## Codebase Discoveries
clip_grad_norm_ returns a DTensor scalar under FSDP2 FULL_SHARD. Elementwise isfinite preserves the wrapper, but torch.distributed.all_reduce does not dispatch c10d.allreduce_ for DTensor in PyTorch 2.11.

